From 3be743989e443693df0c5ec725461196b85d270a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arnaldo Lima <arnaldolimaof@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 07:31:06 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Menu 12 -> 30 fps and motion blur fixed: SSE byte ops, FMA,
 EXP_TEX, RSX copies

SPU on x86 (spu_helpers.h, tests/test_spu_qby_sse.c bit for bit vs _ref):
- rotqby/shlqby/rotqmby and their bi/i forms as one pshufb (they were the
  _ref byte loops, 110-340 instructions; rotqby is the unaligned-scalar
  idiom); shufb indexes host-order quadwords directly; cntb by nibble table.
- spu_fma/fms/fnms in the SPU float mode are one vfmadd under __FMA__
  (operands and product below 2^127). SPU_ASSUME_SPU_FP: lifted code skips
  reading MXCSR on every float op (spu_run_with_halt always sets the mode).
- The LS-load WWS probe moved behind SPU_WWS_RESPROBE; trampoline-step
  diagnostics share one gate.

Render (live draw):
- Fragment programs honour EXP_TEX (OPDEST bit 21): the fetch is expanded
  to [-1,1]. God of War: Ascension's motion blur reads its velocity buffer
  that way; without it "at rest" read as full speed and the whole menu blurred.
  LD_EXP_TEX=0 turns it off.
- Earlier menu work: WPOS origin from SHADER_WINDOW, X32 colour targets,
  depth packed as ARGB8, Y16X16 halves, volume (3D) textures, F12 capture,
  texture bind trace, small main-memory targets written back.
- Texture mutation hash in four lanes; the high-performance GPU is chosen
  and logged.

GCM/SPURS/PPU:
- nv3089 unscaled 32-bit rows copy per row (memmove) unless an SPU holds a
  reservation on the line.
- SPURS_WID_TIMELOG: per policy-module run, with thread CPU time.
- barrier_watch_hit gated inline (15% of the main thread with no watch armed).
- LD_TEXOFF_DBG, SPU_JOB_HIST=2/3, debug console `profip`.

Lifter: --promote-regs (registers in C locals); off by default, no clear gain.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
